                <pb facs="0384" n="319" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg319"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">384.1162 Seventh Day Adventists/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-14T17:00:00+03:00">May 14, 1936—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 14—3:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>340. Italian doctor who is director of sanitation called at Seventh Day Adventist
                    Mission this afternoon and informed them that the Italians desired to take over
                    their hospital. He implied that this was not because of a temporary military
                    emergency but the settled policy of his Government. He was informed that the
                    matter was being referred to the Legation.</p>
                <p>I respectfully suggest that the Department send for L. H. Christian of the
                    General Conference Seventh Day Adventists, Washington, who I understand is
                    thoroughly familiar with the legal aspects of the mission’s tenancy. Contract
                    with the Ethiopian Government shown me still has 16 years to run.</p>
                <p>Should the Italian military authorities in the meantime attempt to take
                    possession of the hospital I shall of course protest.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
